    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d153">

                <pb facs="0267" n="179" sameAs="frus:frus1904/pg179"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Conger to Mr. Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Legation</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Peking,
                                China</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1904-08-25"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 25, 1904</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1690.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herein copies
                    of a letter of the secretary of the bankers’ commission in Shanghai to the dean
                    of the diplomatic corps and its inclosure of a communication from the taotai of
                    Shanghai concerning the payment of the arrears of interest on the indemnity and
                    the question of gold or silver payment.</p>
                <p>The representatives of the powers are not agreed as to the kind of answer to be
                    given, or even as to the necessity of one, and therefore no action is likely to
                    be taken by them.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. H. Conger.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d153-a1.xml" xpointer="d153-a1"/>
